  data: {
    LLM: "Game: FilkÃ³ (Hungarian partnership trick-taker). 32-card German deck, 8 cards per player. Trump set by dealer's bottom card. 120 total points available. Point values: A=11, 10=10, K=4, Over-Knave=3, Under-Knave=2. 8 tricks per round. Lead player (right of dealer) starts anticlockwise. Must follow suit; must trump if void. Winning team captures 61+ points to become Masters; losers become Servants (must deal) until they win.",
    Player: 'Welcome to FilkÃ³! You and your partner compete to capture 61+ points from the 120 available. Cards: Ace (11), Ten (10), King (4), Over-Knave (3), Under-Knave (2). Must follow suit and trump when void. The winning team becomes Masters; the losing team becomes Servants (dealers) until they win.',
    objective: "Capture at least 61 points in a round to be safe; capture major tricks to become the 'Master' (Mester).",
    gameplay: "1. Lead: First player to dealer's right leads.\n2. Must Follow Suit: You must play a card of the suit led.\n3. Must Trump: If you have no cards of the led suit, you ARE forced to play a trump if you have one. You cannot discard if a trump is available.",
    keyRules: [
      "The Master/Servant Loop: When a team wins 6 or more total points/trimmings, they nominate a loser as the 'Servant'. The Servant must stay in that role (dealing every hand) until they win.",
      'Over-Knaves (FilkÃ³): These are always treated as members of the trump suit.',
      "Social Forfeits: Historically, the 'Servant' might have to remove their hat or play while standing.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
